quran[4]{c,v,t}:
  4,20,"If you desire to replace a wife with another wife (by divorcing one to wed another), even if you have given one of them a massive amount of gold (as a bridal gift), do not take anything back from it. Would you take it back by way of accusation and blatant sin?"
  4,21,"How could you take it back while you have had intimate marital relations with each other, and they have (also) taken a firm covenant from you?"
  4,22,"Do not marry any of the women your fathers had married, excluding what has passed previously. It was surely an indecent, hateful and evil custom."
  4,23,"Forbidden to you (for marriage) are your mothers, your daughters, your sisters, your paternal aunts, your maternal aunts, your brother’s daughters, your sister’s daughters, your (foster) mothers who have suckled you, your suckling sisters, mothers of your wives, your stepdaughters who are in your care—(born) from your wives with whom you have consummated the marriage—if you have not consummated the marriage with them, then there is no sin upon you (in marrying them)—the wives of your begotten sons and that you join two sisters (in marriage at one time), except for what has passed. Indeed, Allah is Most Forgiving, All-Merciful."
